# Rule: trust_score_critical_drop
# Category: Trust Violation
# Severity: critical
# Attack Class: trust_degradation
#
# Fires when an agent's real-time trust score from the Rust Trust Graph
# Engine drops below 0.3 — indicating sustained malicious or anomalous
# behaviour across the history, behavior, permissions, and reputation
# dimensions.
#
# The trust_score() PRL function queries the gRPC Trust Engine.  If the
# engine is unreachable it returns 0.5 (neutral), so this rule will NOT
# false-fire during Trust Engine downtime.
#
# Companion rule: trust_score_low_warning (medium severity, threshold 0.5)
# fires earlier as an early-warning signal.

trust_score(event.agent_id, "agent") < 0.3
